Company known for building the biggest ugliest utility truck (11% bigger and stupider than a Dodge Ram \'97 although in this universe it must be called something else). Like most American products, its values were big and powerful. Its mascots were a corn-pipe smoking hillbilly and a brown bear.\
\
With each new model of the truck (what\'92s its name?) .. the hood ornament (a growling brown bear) became bigger and more terrifying. The tuck buying public loved it, identifying with the bear\'92s power and ferocity, and forming the erroneous belief that the bear on the hood was a faithful expression of what was under the hood. (Describe the faulty mechanics of the stupidly large engine and other funny faults of the vehicle).\
\
Slogan: \'93Be the bear. Buy the Chuggabug.\'94\
\
Two things finally combined to kill of the company. Excess of design and wilful ignorance of mechanical lead to the last hood ornament being so large it obscured the driver vision of everything but his own reflection in the oversized rearview mirror. Sadly, if only the hood ornament compromisedthe driver\'92s ability stay in his own lane, or even the right side of the road, or even between the lines of a shopping mall parking space, perhaps\'85 ? But unfortunately the oversized bear on the hood became aerodynamic under highway conditions and made the truck impossible to turn even the gentlest of corners, especially with the accelerator pressed firmly to the floor, which most drivers habitually made sure of. The truck\'92s owners killed themselves at such alarming rate, the company\'92s customer base dwindled to the extent that repeat business was decimated inside of 18 months.\
\
The company may have survived even that if it was not for its President, W. Jay Clinton going down in an ugly public scandal to which his only defence was, \'93I did not have sexual relations with that bear.\'94}